{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfzYPSMoP5E9cxK5ocdfn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm rejecting T-305 on head `d9f34c0d`. Two things must be fixed before it can merge. The first: firstmate can't raise the card that proposes a project's sensitive list, because `fm-decide.sh` refuses the card text that `propose-list` builds.\n\nEverything else the spec asks for is in the diff:\n- **Lists:** the base list in `config.yaml` (CI and workflow files, migrations, SQL, env files, secrets folders), and each project's own list under `projects.<name>.door.sensitive`. A project's list counts only while it matches the record written after the captain's A. The registry refuses a `door` key that would remove the base list.\n- **External tasks:** the pin keeps the door and the lists it was decided with. The plan round, gate 4, the review depth and the pin stop follow the door. The project's own reviewers, CI and branch rules are untouched.\n- **Cannot decide:** a card in en and zh-TW, naming the signal, is raised for each case in the spec: no door, a bad door, no approved list, a hand-edited list, an unclassified path, a listed path on a two-way diff, and `DOOR-CHANGE`. A dispatch card refuses a spec with no door. A scope entry wider than a listed path raises no card.\n- **Tests:** all five required tests exist and fail on base. The two that also pass on base are only side checks, not the tests the change relies on.\n\n## Findings\n\n- **The list-proposal card is refused (must-fix).** In my temporary clone, `fm_door.py propose-list` printed card details, an allocated id was requested with them, and `fm-decide.sh` refused it:\n  ```\n  fm-decide: the card's text breaks the STE rules; nothing was written\n  zh-TW options.A.cons: 清單漏掉的路徑可能走 two-way 流程。 -> Z5 可能\n  ```\n  This is the only violation: with that one string replaced, the request succeeded. The test `approve_list` only checks what `propose-list` prints and never sends the card through `fm-decide`. The kind of problem: card text built in code that tests never check against `fm-decide`'s rules. `card_details` is checked (the stop cards really get requested in the tests); `list_details` never is.\n- **No migration test for pins written before T-305 (must-fix, T-185 rule).** The pin record gains `door_lists` and `door_ask`. The spec says older pins keep their path until a repin. Reading the code, an older external pin stays one-way: `at_gate` returns `EXTERNAL`, `door_kind` stays one-way, and gate 4 and the review skip the door. But no test runs an older external pin under an engine whose config has `door.base`. `test_missing_engine_config_pins_as_before` covers a different case (no engine config at all).\n- **Test guard sweep not extended (follow-up).** `tests/decide.test.sh` now lists `fm_door.py` as a card raiser, but the regex that finds suites reaching a card still doesn't match `fm_door.py` or `fm-worker.sh`. So suites that run `fm-worker.sh` (about 40) are no longer checked for the guard that stops a test from sending real Herdr notifications. The suites I read are guarded (`tests/lib/worker.sh` unsets `HERDR_*`; `door_projects.py` sets `HERDR_ENV=0` in the child environment), so I found no live leak.\n- **Two untested paths (follow-up).** The external dispatch/repin card branch (`fm-decide.sh` passing `--project`/`--state` to `fm_card_spec.py`) is never run in a test. The self repository's CI fail-first check (`fm_door.ci`) applies the base list but not the unclassified-path rule. Gate 4 still runs fail-first locally for such a head, so nothing passes unchecked.\n\n**Executed**\n- `git log --oneline -1 fm/head; git rev-parse HEAD`: the checkout is `d9f34c0d…`, the reviewed head.\n- `sed -n 1040,1140p tests/decide.test.sh`: the regex for suites reaching a card doesn't include `fm_door` or `fm-worker`.\n- `grep HERDR` in `tests/lib.sh`, `tests/lib/worker.sh`, `tests/lib/spec-pins.sh` and the new tests: `worker.sh` unsets `HERDR_*` and exports `HERDR_ENV=0`. `grep -rl fm-worker.sh tests/`: about 40 suites run the worker.\n- `sed -n 215,275p bin/fm-gate.sh` and `grep -n fm_door bin/...`: read gate 4's door branch and every caller.\n- In a temporary clone under `$TMPDIR/rv305`, with `HERDR_ENV=0`: `fm_door.py propose-list` (rc 0), then `fm-decide.sh --allocate` (got `D-firstmate-workflow-T305-1`), then `fm-decide.sh --request … --purpose decision`. The request was refused with the Z5 error on `可能`. A loop then replaced each flagged string in the details file and requested again: there was one violation, and the next request succeeded (rc 0).\n- A `sed` edit of `fm_door.py` in that clone, to test my proposed wording, was denied by the sandbox. So fix 1's wording is not run; `會` is my best guess.\n\n**Read, not run**\n- The external-pin paths in `fm-worker.sh` (the door check before and after pinning, the stop/card hooks, skipping the plan round), `fm-gate.sh` gate 4 and `fm-review.sh`: each checks `has(\"door_lists\")`.\n- `fm_spec_pins.py` writes `door` and `door_lists`, and `door_ask` when undecided, only when the engine config has `door.base`; otherwise it falls back to T-303.\n- `stopped()` releases a pin that couldn't decide only after a captain A; a stop written during a round holds until a repin.\n- `odd_paths` flags renames, submodules and new top-level paths, and skips the round's own `.fm-*` and `design/tasks/` files.\n- The registry refuses `door.base` under a project; the docs in both skills and `design.md` match the code.\n- Older self pins with no `door_lists` read their stored contract text, which has no `door.base`, so their behaviour is unchanged.\n- No background process is started outside `fm_lifeline`; `raise_card` runs `fm-decide` in the foreground with a timeout.\n\n```walk\n{\"intents\":[{\"intent\":1,\"key\":[{\"hunk\":\"config.yaml#R55-89\",\"kind\":\"code\",\"note\":{\"en\":\"The engine config adds the base list that applies to every project.\",\"zh-TW\":\"引擎設定新增適用於每個專案的基本清單。\"}},{\"hunk\":\"bin/lib/fm_door.py#R60-167\",\"kind\":\"code\",\"note\":{\"en\":\"The door module reads the base list and the approved project list.\",\"zh-TW\":\"door 模組讀取基本清單與核准的專案清單。\"}},{\"hunk\":\"bin/lib/fm_registry.py#R115-143\",\"kind\":\"code\",\"note\":{\"en\":\"The registry refuses any project door key other than sensitive.\",\"zh-TW\":\"註冊表拒絕 sensitive 以外的專案 door 鍵。\"}},{\"hunk\":\"tests/door-projects.test.sh#R1-145\",\"kind\":\"test\",\"note\":{\"en\":\"The suite shows that a base-list path makes the head one-way.\",\"zh-TW\":\"測試證明基本清單的路徑讓 head 走 one-way。\"}}]},{\"intent\":2,\"key\":[{\"hunk\":\"bin/lib/fm_spec_pins.py#R527-549\",\"kind\":\"code\",\"note\":{\"en\":\"An external pin keeps its door and its lists.\",\"zh-TW\":\"外部 pin 保存它的 door 與清單。\"}},{\"hunk\":\"bin/fm-worker.sh#R1535-1545\",\"kind\":\"code\",\"note\":{\"en\":\"An external pin written since T-305 follows its door.\",\"zh-TW\":\"T-305 之後寫入的外部 pin 依 door 分流。\"}},{\"hunk\":\"bin/fm-gate.sh#R223-232\",\"kind\":\"code\",\"note\":{\"en\":\"Gate 4 reads the door of an external pin with lists.\",\"zh-TW\":\"gate 4 讀取有清單的外部 pin 的 door。\"}},{\"hunk\":\"tests/lib/door_projects.py#R1-307\",\"kind\":\"test\",\"note\":{\"en\":\"Real external rounds show the two-way path and each card.\",\"zh-TW\":\"真實外部輪次證明 two-way 流程與每張卡。\"}}]},{\"intent\":3,\"key\":[{\"hunk\":\"bin/fm-worker.sh#R82-122\",\"kind\":\"code\",\"note\":{\"en\":\"The launcher holds a pin that cannot decide and raises one card.\",\"zh-TW\":\"啟動器暫停無法判定的 pin 並開一張卡。\"}},{\"hunk\":\"bin/lib/fm_door.py#R451-731\",\"kind\":\"code\",\"note\":{\"en\":\"The door module builds the cards and writes an approved list.\",\"zh-TW\":\"door 模組建立決策卡並寫入核准的清單。\"}},{\"hunk\":\"bin/lib/fm_door.py#R173-322\",\"kind\":\"code\",\"note\":{\"en\":\"A path that no list can classify makes the head one-way.\",\"zh-TW\":\"清單無法分類的路徑讓 head 走 one-way。\"}}]}]}\n```\n\n1. open [must-fix]: The sensitive-list proposal card that `fm_door.py propose-list` builds (`list_details`) is refused by `fm-decide.sh --request`: STE rule Z5 rejects `可能` in `zh-TW options.A.cons`, \"清單漏掉的路徑可能走 two-way 流程。\" So firstmate can't propose a project's list on a captain card, which the acceptance line \"What, where the lists live\" requires. The test helper `approve_list` checks only `propose-list`'s output and never sends it through `fm-decide`. The kind of problem: card text built in code that tests never check against `fm-decide`'s rules. Check every details builder in `fm_door.py` (`list_details` and `card_details`) by a real `--request`.\n   ```text fix-1\n   file: bin/lib/fm_door.py (list_details, zh-TW options.A.cons) and tests/lib/door_projects.py (approve_list)\n   change: replace 可能 with STE-safe wording such as '清單漏掉的路徑會走 two-way 流程。'; in approve_list, allocate an id with `bin/fm-decide.sh --repo <engine> --allocate --task T-305 --project app`, use that id for propose-list, and assert `fm-decide.sh --request <id> --task T-305 --project app --purpose decision --details <propose-list output>` exits 0 and writes state/pending/<id>.json\n   fixes: the new assertion that the proposed list card is accepted by fm-decide --request (today it exits 65 with \"Z5 可能\")\n   fail-first: on the reviewed head the fm-decide request of the propose-list details exits 65 with \"the card's text breaks the STE rules\"\n   ```\n2. open [must-fix]: There is no migration test for a pin written before T-305. The spec says \"Tasks pinned before this change keep their current path until their next repin\", and the T-185 rule needs a test for a changed stored-record format (`door_lists` and `door_ask` are new pin fields). Nothing runs an external pin without `door_lists` under an engine config that has `door.base`, checking that it stays one-way, raises no card, keeps the plan round and that `fm_door.py gate` gives the `EXTERNAL` reason. `test_missing_engine_config_pins_as_before` covers the case with no engine config, not this one. The kind of problem: a format change whose path for existing records is read but never run.\n   ```text fix-2\n   file: tests/lib/door_projects.py (new test) and tests/door-projects.test.sh (new ran() assertion)\n   change: add test_old_external_pin_keeps_one_way: pin T-305 with a two-way spec while the engine config has no door.base (as test_missing_engine_config_pins_as_before does), then restore CONFIG (with door.base) and launch(); assert exit 0, the prompt holds 'This task takes the one-way path' and '# Read first', no state/door-stops or state/pending exists, and `fm_door.py gate` on that pin gives reason 'An external project keeps the one-way path.'; add `assert_eq ok \"$(ran test_old_external_pin_keeps_one_way)\" 'a pin written before T-305 keeps its path'`\n   fixes: the new assertion 'a pin written before T-305 keeps its path'\n   fail-first: reverting the door_lists check in fm_door.at_gate or fm-worker.sh's door_kind block makes the old external pin two-way, and the assertion goes red\n   ```\n3. open [follow-up]: The test guard sweep in `tests/decide.test.sh` now lists `bin/lib/fm_door.py` as a card raiser, but `names` (the regex for suites that reach a card) still doesn't include `fm_door.py` or `fm-worker.sh`. So suites that reach the new door card through `fm-worker.sh` are no longer checked for the guard against real Herdr notifications. The kind of problem: a new indirect card raiser not added to the sweep. The suites I read are guarded today, so I found no live leak.\n   ```text fix-3\n   file: tests/decide.test.sh (the `names=` line near line 1049)\n   change: add `fm_door\\.py|fm-worker\\.sh` to names, and give tests/lib/door_projects.py a top-level os.environ['HERDR_ENV'] = '0' (plus any other newly swept suite that lacks a guard)\n   fixes: '<suite>, a suite that reaches a card, is a tracked file' and its guard assertions now cover the worker suites\n   fail-first: with the names change alone, the guard assertion for tests/lib/door_projects.py fails because its HERDR_ENV=0 is only in a child env dict\n   ```\n4. open [follow-up]: Two paths have no test. First, the external dispatch/repin card branch: `fm-decide.sh` passes `--project`/`--state` to `fm_card_spec.py`, which shows the door decided from the project's approved list. Second, `fm_door.ci` (the self repository's CI fail-first check) applies the base list but not the unclassified-path rule, so a two-way self PR that adds a new top-level folder skips CI fail-first. Gate 4 still catches it locally. The kind of problem: a changed branch with no test, and CI's reading of the door not matching gate 4's.\n   ```text fix-4\n   file: tests/door-projects.test.sh (external card) and bin/lib/fm_door.py ci()\n   change: add an assertion that fm_card_spec.py --config <engine with door.base> --project app --state <state without door-list.json> shows door reason 'Project app has no approved sensitive list. ...'; in ci(), when the base config declares door.base, also treat odd_paths(repo, base_ref, head) as one-way and name the path\n   fixes: new assertions 'an external dispatch card shows the no-list door' and 'CI runs fail-first for an unclassified path'\n   fail-first: reverting the --project/--state branch in fm-decide.sh or fm_card_spec.door shows no door on the external card; ci() today returns two-way for a new top-level folder\n   ```\n\nCRITERIA-COMPLETE:T-305\nREJECT:T-305\nREVIEWER_COMPLETE:T-305"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4113,"cache_read_input_tokens":130888,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4113},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e422fe0c-cbc3-4ea0-9fb7-c9f131da50fd","uuid":"fc81d214-4363-4a3a-9825-08029c5a7535","timestamp":"2026-10-13T16:21:41.732Z","request_id":"req_011CfzYPS7R4GuroCKh2YXiW"}
{"duration_api_ms":152231,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"e422fe0c-cbc3-4ea0-9fb7-c9f131da50fd","total_cost_usd":1.563375,"usage":{"input_tokens":18,"cache_creation_input_tokens":129529,"cache_read_input_tokens":1004955,"output_tokens":16304,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":8655},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":129529,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":18,"outputTokens":16304,"cacheReadInputTokens":1004955,"cacheCreationInputTokens":129529,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.563375,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":8655,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_019JEDDXM61yaWGKRdq8e9Va","tool_input":{"command":"cd \"$TMPDIR/rv305/eng\"; export HERDR_ENV=0 FM_ROOT=\"$PWD\"; rm -f state/pending/*; sed -i '' \"s/cons='清單漏掉的路徑可能走 two-way 流程。'/cons='清單漏掉的路徑會走 two-way 流程。'/\" bin/lib/fm_door.py; python3 bin/lib/fm_door.py propose-list --state state --project firstmate-workflow --task T-305 --id D-firstmate-workflow-T305-2 --globs '[\"src/keys/**\"]' --config config.yaml > ../d2.json; id=$(bin/fm-decide.sh --repo \"$PWD\" --allocate --task T-305); bin/fm-decide.sh --repo \"$PWD\" --request \"$id\" --task T-305 --purpose decision --details ../d2.json 2>&1 | tail -2; grep -n \"可能\" bin/lib/fm_door.py","description":"Verify the proposed zh-TW wording passes fm-decide"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":9,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I'm rejecting T-305 on head `d9f34c0d`. Two things must be fixed before it can merge. The first: firstmate can't raise the card that proposes a project's sensitive list, because `fm-decide.sh` refuses the card text that `propose-list` builds.\n\nEverything else the spec asks for is in the diff:\n- **Lists:** the base list in `config.yaml` (CI and workflow files, migrations, SQL, env files, secrets folders), and each project's own list under `projects.<name>.door.sensitive`. A project's list counts only while it matches the record written after the captain's A. The registry refuses a `door` key that would remove the base list.\n- **External tasks:** the pin keeps the door and the lists it was decided with. The plan round, gate 4, the review depth and the pin stop follow the door. The project's own reviewers, CI and branch rules are untouched.\n- **Cannot decide:** a card in en and zh-TW, naming the signal, is raised for each case in the spec: no door, a bad door, no approved list, a hand-edited list, an unclassified path, a listed path on a two-way diff, and `DOOR-CHANGE`. A dispatch card refuses a spec with no door. A scope entry wider than a listed path raises no card.\n- **Tests:** all five required tests exist and fail on base. The two that also pass on base are only side checks, not the tests the change relies on.\n\n## Findings\n\n- **The list-proposal card is refused (must-fix).** In my temporary clone, `fm_door.py propose-list` printed card details, an allocated id was requested with them, and `fm-decide.sh` refused it:\n  ```\n  fm-decide: the card's text breaks the STE rules; nothing was written\n  zh-TW options.A.cons: 清單漏掉的路徑可能走 two-way 流程。 -> Z5 可能\n  ```\n  This is the only violation: with that one string replaced, the request succeeded. The test `approve_list` only checks what `propose-list` prints and never sends the card through `fm-decide`. The kind of problem: card text built in code that tests never check against `fm-decide`'s rules. `card_details` is checked (the stop cards really get requested in the tests); `list_details` never is.\n- **No migration test for pins written before T-305 (must-fix, T-185 rule).** The pin record gains `door_lists` and `door_ask`. The spec says older pins keep their path until a repin. Reading the code, an older external pin stays one-way: `at_gate` returns `EXTERNAL`, `door_kind` stays one-way, and gate 4 and the review skip the door. But no test runs an older external pin under an engine whose config has `door.base`. `test_missing_engine_config_pins_as_before` covers a different case (no engine config at all).\n- **Test guard sweep not extended (follow-up).** `tests/decide.test.sh` now lists `fm_door.py` as a card raiser, but the regex that finds suites reaching a card still doesn't match `fm_door.py` or `fm-worker.sh`. So suites that run `fm-worker.sh` (about 40) are no longer checked for the guard that stops a test from sending real Herdr notifications. The suites I read are guarded (`tests/lib/worker.sh` unsets `HERDR_*`; `door_projects.py` sets `HERDR_ENV=0` in the child environment), so I found no live leak.\n- **Two untested paths (follow-up).** The external dispatch/repin card branch (`fm-decide.sh` passing `--project`/`--state` to `fm_card_spec.py`) is never run in a test. The self repository's CI fail-first check (`fm_door.ci`) applies the base list but not the unclassified-path rule. Gate 4 still runs fail-first locally for such a head, so nothing passes unchecked.\n\n**Executed**\n- `git log --oneline -1 fm/head; git rev-parse HEAD`: the checkout is `d9f34c0d…`, the reviewed head.\n- `sed -n 1040,1140p tests/decide.test.sh`: the regex for suites reaching a card doesn't include `fm_door` or `fm-worker`.\n- `grep HERDR` in `tests/lib.sh`, `tests/lib/worker.sh`, `tests/lib/spec-pins.sh` and the new tests: `worker.sh` unsets `HERDR_*` and exports `HERDR_ENV=0`. `grep -rl fm-worker.sh tests/`: about 40 suites run the worker.\n- `sed -n 215,275p bin/fm-gate.sh` and `grep -n fm_door bin/...`: read gate 4's door branch and every caller.\n- In a temporary clone under `$TMPDIR/rv305`, with `HERDR_ENV=0`: `fm_door.py propose-list` (rc 0), then `fm-decide.sh --allocate` (got `D-firstmate-workflow-T305-1`), then `fm-decide.sh --request … --purpose decision`. The request was refused with the Z5 error on `可能`. A loop then replaced each flagged string in the details file and requested again: there was one violation, and the next request succeeded (rc 0).\n- A `sed` edit of `fm_door.py` in that clone, to test my proposed wording, was denied by the sandbox. So fix 1's wording is not run; `會` is my best guess.\n\n**Read, not run**\n- The external-pin paths in `fm-worker.sh` (the door check before and after pinning, the stop/card hooks, skipping the plan round), `fm-gate.sh` gate 4 and `fm-review.sh`: each checks `has(\"door_lists\")`.\n- `fm_spec_pins.py` writes `door` and `door_lists`, and `door_ask` when undecided, only when the engine config has `door.base`; otherwise it falls back to T-303.\n- `stopped()` releases a pin that couldn't decide only after a captain A; a stop written during a round holds until a repin.\n- `odd_paths` flags renames, submodules and new top-level paths, and skips the round's own `.fm-*` and `design/tasks/` files.\n- The registry refuses `door.base` under a project; the docs in both skills and `design.md` match the code.\n- Older self pins with no `door_lists` read their stored contract text, which has no `door.base`, so their behaviour is unchanged.\n- No background process is started outside `fm_lifeline`; `raise_card` runs `fm-decide` in the foreground with a timeout.\n\n```walk\n{\"intents\":[{\"intent\":1,\"key\":[{\"hunk\":\"config.yaml#R55-89\",\"kind\":\"code\",\"note\":{\"en\":\"The engine config adds the base list that applies to every project.\",\"zh-TW\":\"引擎設定新增適用於每個專案的基本清單。\"}},{\"hunk\":\"bin/lib/fm_door.py#R60-167\",\"kind\":\"code\",\"note\":{\"en\":\"The door module reads the base list and the approved project list.\",\"zh-TW\":\"door 模組讀取基本清單與核准的專案清單。\"}},{\"hunk\":\"bin/lib/fm_registry.py#R115-143\",\"kind\":\"code\",\"note\":{\"en\":\"The registry refuses any project door key other than sensitive.\",\"zh-TW\":\"註冊表拒絕 sensitive 以外的專案 door 鍵。\"}},{\"hunk\":\"tests/door-projects.test.sh#R1-145\",\"kind\":\"test\",\"note\":{\"en\":\"The suite shows that a base-list path makes the head one-way.\",\"zh-TW\":\"測試證明基本清單的路徑讓 head 走 one-way。\"}}]},{\"intent\":2,\"key\":[{\"hunk\":\"bin/lib/fm_spec_pins.py#R527-549\",\"kind\":\"code\",\"note\":{\"en\":\"An external pin keeps its door and its lists.\",\"zh-TW\":\"外部 pin 保存它的 door 與清單。\"}},{\"hunk\":\"bin/fm-worker.sh#R1535-1545\",\"kind\":\"code\",\"note\":{\"en\":\"An external pin written since T-305 follows its door.\",\"zh-TW\":\"T-305 之後寫入的外部 pin 依 door 分流。\"}},{\"hunk\":\"bin/fm-gate.sh#R223-232\",\"kind\":\"code\",\"note\":{\"en\":\"Gate 4 reads the door of an external pin with lists.\",\"zh-TW\":\"gate 4 讀取有清單的外部 pin 的 door。\"}},{\"hunk\":\"tests/lib/door_projects.py#R1-307\",\"kind\":\"test\",\"note\":{\"en\":\"Real external rounds show the two-way path and each card.\",\"zh-TW\":\"真實外部輪次證明 two-way 流程與每張卡。\"}}]},{\"intent\":3,\"key\":[{\"hunk\":\"bin/fm-worker.sh#R82-122\",\"kind\":\"code\",\"note\":{\"en\":\"The launcher holds a pin that cannot decide and raises one card.\",\"zh-TW\":\"啟動器暫停無法判定的 pin 並開一張卡。\"}},{\"hunk\":\"bin/lib/fm_door.py#R451-731\",\"kind\":\"code\",\"note\":{\"en\":\"The door module builds the cards and writes an approved list.\",\"zh-TW\":\"door 模組建立決策卡並寫入核准的清單。\"}},{\"hunk\":\"bin/lib/fm_door.py#R173-322\",\"kind\":\"code\",\"note\":{\"en\":\"A path that no list can classify makes the head one-way.\",\"zh-TW\":\"清單無法分類的路徑讓 head 走 one-way。\"}}]}]}\n```\n\n1. open [must-fix]: The sensitive-list proposal card that `fm_door.py propose-list` builds (`list_details`) is refused by `fm-decide.sh --request`: STE rule Z5 rejects `可能` in `zh-TW options.A.cons`, \"清單漏掉的路徑可能走 two-way 流程。\" So firstmate can't propose a project's list on a captain card, which the acceptance line \"What, where the lists live\" requires. The test helper `approve_list` checks only `propose-list`'s output and never sends it through `fm-decide`. The kind of problem: card text built in code that tests never check against `fm-decide`'s rules. Check every details builder in `fm_door.py` (`list_details` and `card_details`) by a real `--request`.\n   ```text fix-1\n   file: bin/lib/fm_door.py (list_details, zh-TW options.A.cons) and tests/lib/door_projects.py (approve_list)\n   change: replace 可能 with STE-safe wording such as '清單漏掉的路徑會走 two-way 流程。'; in approve_list, allocate an id with `bin/fm-decide.sh --repo <engine> --allocate --task T-305 --project app`, use that id for propose-list, and assert `fm-decide.sh --request <id> --task T-305 --project app --purpose decision --details <propose-list output>` exits 0 and writes state/pending/<id>.json\n   fixes: the new assertion that the proposed list card is accepted by fm-decide --request (today it exits 65 with \"Z5 可能\")\n   fail-first: on the reviewed head the fm-decide request of the propose-list details exits 65 with \"the card's text breaks the STE rules\"\n   ```\n2. open [must-fix]: There is no migration test for a pin written before T-305. The spec says \"Tasks pinned before this change keep their current path until their next repin\", and the T-185 rule needs a test for a changed stored-record format (`door_lists` and `door_ask` are new pin fields). Nothing runs an external pin without `door_lists` under an engine config that has `door.base`, checking that it stays one-way, raises no card, keeps the plan round and that `fm_door.py gate` gives the `EXTERNAL` reason. `test_missing_engine_config_pins_as_before` covers the case with no engine config, not this one. The kind of problem: a format change whose path for existing records is read but never run.\n   ```text fix-2\n   file: tests/lib/door_projects.py (new test) and tests/door-projects.test.sh (new ran() assertion)\n   change: add test_old_external_pin_keeps_one_way: pin T-305 with a two-way spec while the engine config has no door.base (as test_missing_engine_config_pins_as_before does), then restore CONFIG (with door.base) and launch(); assert exit 0, the prompt holds 'This task takes the one-way path' and '# Read first', no state/door-stops or state/pending exists, and `fm_door.py gate` on that pin gives reason 'An external project keeps the one-way path.'; add `assert_eq ok \"$(ran test_old_external_pin_keeps_one_way)\" 'a pin written before T-305 keeps its path'`\n   fixes: the new assertion 'a pin written before T-305 keeps its path'\n   fail-first: reverting the door_lists check in fm_door.at_gate or fm-worker.sh's door_kind block makes the old external pin two-way, and the assertion goes red\n   ```\n3. open [follow-up]: The test guard sweep in `tests/decide.test.sh` now lists `bin/lib/fm_door.py` as a card raiser, but `names` (the regex for suites that reach a card) still doesn't include `fm_door.py` or `fm-worker.sh`. So suites that reach the new door card through `fm-worker.sh` are no longer checked for the guard against real Herdr notifications. The kind of problem: a new indirect card raiser not added to the sweep. The suites I read are guarded today, so I found no live leak.\n   ```text fix-3\n   file: tests/decide.test.sh (the `names=` line near line 1049)\n   change: add `fm_door\\.py|fm-worker\\.sh` to names, and give tests/lib/door_projects.py a top-level os.environ['HERDR_ENV'] = '0' (plus any other newly swept suite that lacks a guard)\n   fixes: '<suite>, a suite that reaches a card, is a tracked file' and its guard assertions now cover the worker suites\n   fail-first: with the names change alone, the guard assertion for tests/lib/door_projects.py fails because its HERDR_ENV=0 is only in a child env dict\n   ```\n4. open [follow-up]: Two paths have no test. First, the external dispatch/repin card branch: `fm-decide.sh` passes `--project`/`--state` to `fm_card_spec.py`, which shows the door decided from the project's approved list. Second, `fm_door.ci` (the self repository's CI fail-first check) applies the base list but not the unclassified-path rule, so a two-way self PR that adds a new top-level folder skips CI fail-first. Gate 4 still catches it locally. The kind of problem: a changed branch with no test, and CI's reading of the door not matching gate 4's.\n   ```text fix-4\n   file: tests/door-projects.test.sh (external card) and bin/lib/fm_door.py ci()\n   change: add an assertion that fm_card_spec.py --config <engine with door.base> --project app --state <state without door-list.json> shows door reason 'Project app has no approved sensitive list. ...'; in ci(), when the base config declares door.base, also treat odd_paths(repo, base_ref, head) as one-way and name the path\n   fixes: new assertions 'an external dispatch card shows the no-list door' and 'CI runs fail-first for an unclassified path'\n   fail-first: reverting the --project/--state branch in fm-decide.sh or fm_card_spec.door shows no door on the external card; ci() today returns two-way for a new top-level folder\n   ```\n\nCRITERIA-COMPLETE:T-305\nREJECT:T-305\nREVIEWER_COMPLETE:T-305","ttft_ms":43681,"type":"result","duration_ms":157643,"uuid":"900ee23a-d7d8-4078-991e-80b70ed15872","ttft_stream_ms":1685,"time_to_request_ms":73,"first_content_frame_ms":1686,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
